  "worked_solution": "The denominators are $12$ and $4.$ We can make a common denominator of $12$ by splitting the shape on the right into $3$ parts horizontally:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14155061/assets/1d05074d23c48a2ff9604d5a1aec5521c0fb043ebeed9424f7182e480404771d.png)\n\nSo, our division problem now is\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{12}÷\\frac{9}{12}.\n$$\n\nSince the denominators are equal, this is equivalent to\n\n$$\n7÷9=\\frac{7}{9}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{12}÷\\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{\\boxed{\\,7\\,}}{9}\\,.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing number is $7.$",
